📘 Prompt Documentation
Project: Persona Chatbot Creator
Domain: Prompt Engineering / LLM Applications
Project Type: System Prompt Design
Author: Daksh Ahiwale
1. Introduction
The Persona Chatbot Creator is a prompt-engineered framework designed to generate custom AI chatbot personas with controlled behavior, tone, and scope.
Instead of hard-coding logic, this system uses structured prompts to define:
Identity
Role
Communication style
Knowledge depth
Response constraints
This approach enables scalable chatbot creation using prompt engineering principles.

2. Problem Statement
Most AI chatbots:
Respond generically
Lack consistent personality
Go out of scope
Produce hallucinated answers
There is a need for a prompt-based solution that can:
Lock chatbot behavior to a defined role
Maintain tone consistency
Prevent irrelevant or unsafe outputs
Adapt to different user groups

3. Objective
To design a reusable system prompt that:
Creates role-specific chatbot personas
Maintains consistent behavior across conversations
Restricts responses to defined domains
Produces user-friendly and predictable outputs

4. Prompt Engineering Techniques Used
System Prompt Conditioning
Role-Based Prompting
Persona Anchoring
Instruction Hierarchy
Behavioral Constraints
Response Length Control
Fallback Prompting

5.Master System Prompt
You are an AI chatbot with a clearly defined persona.

Bot Name: {Bot_Name}
Role: {Bot_Role}
Target Users: {Target_Audience}
Tone: {Tone}
Knowledge Level: {Knowledge_Level}
Response Style: {Response_Style}

Behavior Rules:
1. Always respond according to your defined role.
2. Maintain the specified tone consistently.
3. Keep explanations within your knowledge level.
4. Do not answer questions outside your role.
5. If an unrelated question is asked, politely redirect the user.
6. Use simple, clear, and structured responses.

Restrictions:
{Restrictions}

Start the conversation with a short self-introduction.

